**Definition (Product regions and complex operations)** · `def:nrz:cas-solving-design-regions`

Product regions retain exact ordered coordinates and reuse GuardTrue, GuardFalse, Union, Meet, Difference, Empty and Ambient. A total coefficient region T lying over a Real stratum S stores the exact family and stratum; checked projection membership proves containment in the preimage of S. RealSigns and zero/nonzero covers require defined expressions and exact local evidence, without claiming that the rational affine interval decider decides multivariate signs. Unknown cells remain until emptiness is proved (`rule:nrz:cas-symbol-sorts-stratum-evidence`).

Every expression has an explicitly checked AmbientSpace determined by its operator signature and operands. Own-space arithmetic has no placement-induced cases. Mixed Real/Complex operators elaborate to native Cases with local FamilyExpression bodies and explicit Real-in-Complex placement uses. Incidence is `RealPart(q)=t`, `ImagPart(q)=0` with Complex query location q and local Real t; the original Real declaration is evaluated by same-Real substitution. The independent Complex coordinate remains unrestricted. Multiple Real operands compose by meets of their placement pieces; no missing arm is filled (`def:nrz:cas-symbol-sorts-real-placement`), (`def:nrz:cas-symbol-sorts-family-arithmetic`).

A complete piece theorem quantifies over its exact coefficient stratum and original unknown domain, with original denominator checks and no further roots there. Closing its context retains that region. Only a larger requested-domain claim additionally consumes base and fibre covers; the latter is quantified for every base point. Complete pieces survive BaseCoveragePending or FibreCoveragePending. A proved outside-support query returns NoApplicablePiece with exclusion evidence, while unknown membership returns PieceMembershipPending. Neither is an empty-root theorem (`def:nrz:cas-symbol-sorts-piece-completeness`).

Conjugate preserves Complex sort; RealPart/ImagPart return distinct Real expressions. Component reassembly uses the registered local placement agreement, never a scalar inclusion or a retyped declaration. RootValue and ExactCoefficient retain their explicit selected-root or value/map attachments, same-sort scopes and existence/definedness dependencies. Real requests stay in Real, and Real-with-Complex original dependencies get RealProblemHasComplexSymbol. Remove the separate Complex header lift, reverse restriction and private transported-parameter realness convention; retain same-sort SolutionTransport and actual ConjugationTransport conclusions (`sec:nrz:cas-symbol-sorts-wire-policy`).

