## Requests, judgments and outcomes · `sec:nrz:cas-solving-design-judgments`

**Definition (Quantifiers and residuals)** · `def:nrz:cas-solving-design-quantifiers`

Every SolveStatement is inside the existing Judgment { context, layer, space, statement, residuals }. Algebraic solving uses Layer::Logic with no distribution Space; scalar ambient, products, base/family and placements are explicit structural references. Region theorems quantify over all admissible parameters on their exact piece and explicit binders. Base-only predicates cannot silently depend on fibre coordinates. Consistency stays Unknown unless proved. A complete piece discharges every local sign, unit, existence/count obligation. A conditional theorem retains its explicit assumptions and cannot be advertised as a completed piece; an outstanding larger-domain cover is separate. Guarded residuals retain home context, region and scope, and closure never widens the theorem (`rule:nrz:cas-symbol-sorts-stratum-evidence`).

