**Definition (Policy, availability and dominance)** · `def:nrz:cas-solving-design-policy`

The logical v10 vector retains the 59 pre-solving weights and 17 retained solving weights, removes solve.real-restrict and adds coeff.evaluate = 4, real.sign = 2, real.root-count = 8 and real.cell-exists = 2; total 80 keys. Retained semantic versions stay v1 because their propositions are unchanged. Availability is a separate exact bitmap with restriction removed; an unavailable checker refuses and no producer advertises it. Witnesses carry only actually reached rules; expanded family recipes pay their actual positive primitive costs. Space/placement specification versions participate in portable and policy identity, so no old plan or shortcut can authorize a changed definition (`def:nrz:cas-symbol-sorts-wire-replacement`).

A solve state contains the original problem, exact declaration/ambient/placement and base/family/stratum structure, goal/form, full context/residuals, actual coefficient maps and selections, checked piece facts, separate pending cover obligations, strategy cursor, DAG and usage. Sort routing is a bounded dependency scan before expensive search, charging Work, Depth, payload and graph limits with no coefficient/orbit work; it preserves every retained declared-space producer and refuses only the specified contradictions/capabilities (`alg:nrz:cas-symbol-sorts-routing`), (`arg:nrz:cas-symbol-sorts-route-preservation`). Dominance compares identical semantic keys and proof strength, including capability/policy identities; no smaller expression dominates a stronger theorem or a sibling region.

The Complex scheduler retains cost_quota = 4 and progress_quota = 1, degree drop, generic subleading translation, binomials, canonical cyclic characters and partition seeds. Skip orbits no smaller than the source degree before resolvent expansion; recurse only on smaller degrees and recover via checked linear equivalence and discovered pairings. The Real scheduler separately performs same-Real composition/division, degree/sign strata, generically derived radicals and Sturm counts/cells (`alg:nrz:cas-symbol-sorts-real-cubic`). Its bounded ordered-field sign rules and real root existence are explicit additions, not renamed Complex discovery. Both share cumulative ledgers across every branch and failed attempt.

For degree n the cyclic seed is Σⱼ ζₙ^(kj)yⱼ for k = 1,…,n − 1. Formal root variables occupy the bound Polynomial frame; they are not extra adjoined computational tower levels. Vieta hypotheses are explicitly scoped and eliminated in the coefficient substitution proof before the radical construction, whose coefficient base remains the original domain. Powers 1 through n/gcd(n,k) are offered in increasing order; the exponent bound follows from the cyclic character order. All S_n orbit generators are adjacent transpositions; closure is checked on the full finite orbit. For n = 3 the two characters, powers 1,2,3 and six permutations are reached by this schedule, and the first lower-degree orbit has size two. The degree-two recursive request uses the same translation and binomial method, yielding completing-the-square as a checked lemma. The product of the two degree-one characters is the first nontrivial cross-character product. Its checked value provides the linked selection; the inverse character matrix supplies the roots. These are consequences of the generic seed order and arithmetic, not production lookup constants.

**Rule (Blind discovery audit)** · `rule:nrz:cas-solving-design-blind`

Pin each original fixture independently, including declaration fields, initial maps and original request forms. Five fixtures declare Complex a,b,c,d,x and retain Radicals; the Real fixture currently asks Radicals but S3 visibly revises it to AnyExact/RealExact. Record revision, exact manifest/capability/policy, unchanged limits, first fault path/domain/map/region/schema, generation/replay ledgers and actual reached DAG. Never call an aggregate exact-coefficients fault a missing Real bridge (`req:nrz:cas-symbol-sorts-complex-diagnosis`). Successful Complex traces retain generic orbit/reduction/recovery evidence; Real traces retain real sign/count and radical/cell evidence with no Complex relation in coverage. Independent oracles and fresh expected-claim replay are required for all six (`tab:nrz:cas-symbol-sorts-six-tests`).

