For the blind examples, independently multiply the final factors and differentiate the original polynomial. Bombelli must check (2 + i)³ = 2 + 11i, uv = 5 and roots 4, −2 ± √3. The casus example x³ − 3x + 1 must check the cyclotomic relation t⁶ + t³ + 1 for a ninth root of unity, the three rational sign intervals and irreducibility by the rational-root test in degree three; no floating sample certifies equality or completeness. The repeated example must check (x − 1)²(x + 2), gcd/Bezout and derivative multiplicities. The p = 0 example must check (x + 2)(x² − 2x + 4) = x³ + 8 without dividing by a zero U. The general symbolic test checks the original a,b,c,d polynomial after the affine shift and retains every coefficient stratum. The impossibility of an all-real radical tower for the casus example is mathematical commentary from the concept's cited theorem, not an executable GenericGaloisObstruction result in this release.

Every primitive has one valid supplied-certificate fixture before its producer is enabled, plus a false-premise/certificate mutation and fresh-store replay. Every new cumulative/peak limit has a small exactly measured boundary fixture. Public success tests also inspect the witness's residuals, used hypotheses, solution strength and presentation; checking only a pretty-printed formula is insufficient. Existing scalar, piecewise and distribution tests remain required after the format replacement. The four-layer inventory and gate requirements follow (`dec:nrz:cas-piecewise-design-test-layout`) and (`rule:nrz:required-verification`). No Rust tests or repository gate are claimed to have run in this documentation round.

