**Rule (Release findings and scope boundaries)** · `rule:nrz:cas-solving-design-findings`

The coordinated solving and piecewise specifications now incorporate ambient-relative placement, local-space arms, per-piece completeness, AnyExact/RealExact and removal of RealRestriction. The code/codec/policy replacements remain S1–S4 work; this documentation commit makes no capability claim. Existing README/census and registry inventories need their normal implementation-time updates. The five current Complex refusals need the first operation diagnosis, not a sort explanation; symbolic sign production and complete successful resource costs still need evidence (`open:nrz:cas-symbol-sorts-review-items`).

This revision changes only the four owned specifications and their templates. It adds no code, dependency, parser, compatibility reader, new scalar-space algorithm, general factorization or numerical client behavior. RealRestriction removal and the new finite-evaluation/real-sign/Sturm trust boundaries are explicit decisions for implementation. The generic quintic impossibility checker stays deferred. Bibliographic verification caveats remain those of the concept; no external implementation or test suite supplied this revision.
